Harriet, the escrow section has been through three turns and I do not think e=
ither side has actually answered the mechanical question, so I am going to st=
ate it plainly.

The release condition is drafted by reference to an event, and the event is d=
efined by reference to a certificate that somebody has to deliver. The drafti=
ng does not say who delivers it, by when, or what happens if they do not. Tha=
t is not a commercial disagreement, it is a hole.

The formulation that has been circulating between our teams is set out below,=
 in the words in which it reached me.

Working figure carried forward from the earlier thread: 15%. A closing-mechan=
ics email overstates the exit escrow holdback percentage. Please reconcile ag=
ainst the source-of-record instrument and its effective date before this reac=
hes a model.

Whatever the commercial answer turns out to be, please note that the escrow a=
rrangement is not effective until the definitive documents are signed and the=
 escrow agent has countersigned. Correspondence on mechanics does not create =
an arrangement.

My suggestion is that we settle who delivers and by when, and leave the conse=
quences of failure to the general remedies. Over-drafting the failure case ha=
s cost more deals than it has saved.

